# Xcode / Swift .gitignore
# Based on github/gitignore Swift + Xcode templates

## User settings & state
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xccheckout

## Build artifacts
build/
DerivedData/
*.moved-aside
*.hmap
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM

# NOTE: The project is Xcode-managed and committed (see README). We still ignore
# per-user state below; only the shared project structure is tracked.

## Swift Package Manager
.build/
.swiftpm/

## CocoaPods / Carthage (unused, but ignore if added later)
Pods/
Carthage/Build/

## Local signing identity — see Signing.xcconfig.
Local.xcconfig

## Editor / tooling local state
.claude/
.agents/

## Face-model conversion tooling — local, one-time (scripts/convert_adaface.py,
## scripts/convert_sface.py). Neither the large source models (AdaFace .ckpt
## ~700 MB, SFace .onnx), the Python venv, nor the converted 83 MB .mlpackage
## are tracked (non-commercial weights + repo bloat). Regenerate the model
## locally with convert_adaface.py; the app gates on its presence in Resources/.
.venv/
*.onnx
*.ckpt
__pycache__/
PhotoSwipe/Resources/FaceEmbedding.mlpackage/

## MobileCLIP S2 research-model conversion. Source and tokenizer files are
## tracked; everything scripts/convert_mobileclip.py writes (model weights,
## Core ML derivatives, parity fixtures, provenance) is local. The app gates
## Search on the provenance file being present in Resources/.
PhotoSwipe/Resources/MobileCLIPS2Image.mlpackage/
PhotoSwipe/Resources/MobileCLIPS2Text.mlpackage/
PhotoSwipe/Resources/mobileclip-provenance.json
PhotoSwipeTests/Fixtures/MobileCLIP/
docs/mobileclip-provenance.json
mobileclip_s2.pt

## SigLIP 2, the distributable alternative (CC-BY 4.0 weights). Same rule: the
## converter (scripts/convert_siglip2.py) and the Swift tokenizer are tracked,
## everything the conversion produces is local.
PhotoSwipe/Resources/SigLIP2Image.mlpackage/
PhotoSwipe/Resources/SigLIP2Text.mlpackage/
PhotoSwipe/Resources/siglip2-vocab.json
PhotoSwipe/Resources/siglip2-provenance.json
PhotoSwipeTests/Fixtures/SigLIP2/
docs/siglip2-provenance.json

## macOS
.DS_Store

## Misc
*.swp
*.save

## Markdown — only the README and license notes are tracked. Version briefs,
## engineering notes (docs/), and personal scratchpads stay local.
*.md
!README.md
!THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md
!LEARNINGS.md
docs/

## Claude skills lock (local tooling state, like .agents/)
skills-lock.json
